  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "The midpoints of the sides of an equilateral triangle are joined, forming a second triangle. The midpoints of the sides of the second triangle are joined to form a third triangle, and so on. Given that the perimeter of the original triangle is 6, find:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "the sum of the perimeters of all of the triangles",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$12$ units",
          "worked": "Joining the midpoints halves each side length, so the perimeters form a geometric series with first term $6$ and common ratio $\\frac12$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=\\frac{6}{1-\\frac12}\\\\P&=12\\text{ units}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the sum of the areas of all of the triangles.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{4\\sqrt3}{3}$ square units\n\nThe side lengths halve, so successive areas have ratio $\\frac14$.",
          "worked": "The original triangle has side length $2$. Its altitude is $h$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}h&=\\sqrt{2^2-1^2}\\\\h&=\\sqrt3\\\\A_1&=\\frac12\\times2\\times\\sqrt3\\\\A_1&=\\sqrt3.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe triangles are similar with side-length ratio $\\frac12$, so their area ratio is $\\left(\\frac12\\right)^2=\\frac14$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{1-\\frac14}\\\\A&=\\frac{4\\sqrt3}{3}\\text{ square units}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      }
    ]
  },
